--- /dev/null
+++ b/android/native/reown_wcpay/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# Maintained WCPay 0.10.60 Android native module
+
+The local Maven module at `maven/com/github/reown-com/yttrium/yttrium-wcpay/0.10.60/` preserves the selected official AAR's Kotlin `classes.jar`, manifest, resources, directory entries and POM. Only its four `libuniffi_yttrium_wcpay.so` members are replaced with native libraries linked from exact Yttrium commit `fc2dc73ae1e1af2b29363c6d239c0e3a19ec8f7c` and `Cargo.lock` SHA256 `ac084735f19fd9796dcce2cf672f6e616f43798601bfd0f22e1e7e8a85e45f2b` using the WCPay release profile and the recorded maintained Rust/NDK toolchain. The two generated Kotlin files from the candidate are byte-identical to the official 0.10.60 release files, including UniFFI contract version 30 and all 12 checksums. `scripts/build_reown_wcpay_android.py` records the source build; `scripts/build_reown_wcpay_maven.py` guards this package's official inputs and candidate member hashes.
+
+The official POM is copied bytewise. The Gradle `.module` preserves its original component and dependency graph, including JNA 5.17.0; only the API/runtime AAR size and digests are updated. `android/build.gradle.kts` selects this repository exclusively for `com.github.reown-com.yttrium:yttrium-wcpay:0.10.60`. This maintained local coordinate does not change the Flutter Pay or wallet API.
+
+`licenses/` retains the supplier Apache-2.0 LICENSE and actual license files from compiled native dependencies where Cargo metadata was incomplete (`ring 0.16.20`, `curve25519-dalek-derive 0.1.1`) plus vendored OpenSSL source/license files. The task-owned compiled dependency inventory and original license-file hashes are retained in the Task 16F evidence directory. This set is provenance evidence; full third-party notice clearance remains part of release review.
+
+The selected AAR and its four native members require the synthetic JNA/UniFFI runtime fixture, and the final app package requires whole-artifact alignment and device checks after the other Task 16F native groups are integrated.
